---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
import { getLegalDocument } from '../content/read';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Privacy notice', path: '/privacy/' }];
const mailto = `mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}?subject=Privacy%20request`;
const legalDocument = await getLegalDocument('privacy');
if (!legalDocument) throw new Error('Privacy content is missing.');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${legalDocument.title} — draft`}
  description={legalDocument.description}
  noindex={legalDocument.status !== 'approved'}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy notice' }]} />
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Draft for legal review"
    title={legalDocument.title}
    intro="This notice explains how the current website build is designed to handle information. It is not yet an approved legal notice and must be reviewed against the final entity, jurisdiction and services before launch."
    compact
  />

  <div class="shell legal-status" role="note" aria-label="Document status">
    <strong>Status: {legalDocument.status.replace('-', ' ')}</strong>
    <span>Last reviewed {legalDocument.lastReviewed}. Operator identity, registered address, applicable law, hosting location and named processors remain to be confirmed.</span>
  </div>

  <div class="shell legal-layout">
    <aside aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="eyebrow">On this page</p>
      <nav>
        <a href="#scope">Scope and responsibility</a>
        <a href="#collection">Information collected</a>
        <a href="#use">How information is used</a>
        <a href="#sharing">Sharing and processing</a>
        <a href="#retention">Retention and security</a>
        <a href="#choices">Your choices</a>
        <a href="#cookies">Cookies and analytics</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <article class="legal-copy">
      <section id="scope" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>1. Scope and responsibility</h2>
        <p class="cms-summary">{legalDocument.body}</p>
        <p>This draft applies to the public pages and enquiry forms on this Impact Sol. website. Impact Sol. is currently described as an initiative being established. The organisation legally responsible for personal information—and its address and registration details—must be inserted after it is confirmed.</p>
        <p>The contact route for privacy questions during this pre-launch stage is <a href={mailto}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="collection" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>2. Information the website may collect</h2>
        <h3>Information you submit</h3>
        <p>The general, partnership and maker or initiative forms collect your name, email address and message. Depending on the form, you may also choose to provide an organisation, phone number, country or region, and website or public-profile link.</p>
        <p>Do not submit passwords, payment information, health details, identity documents, confidential business material or other sensitive information through these enquiry forms.</p>
        <h3>Technical and anti-abuse information</h3>
        <p>Netlify may process limited request information needed to deliver the site, filter spam, diagnose failures and protect the forms. This can include timestamps, request headers and network information. The final hosting setup and log retention must be documented before launch.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="use" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>3. How information is intended to be used</h2>
        <p>Enquiry information is intended to be used only to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>receive, review and respond to the message you send;</li>
          <li>route a partnership or maker enquiry to an appropriate person;</li>
          <li>maintain the security and reliability of the enquiry service;</li>
          <li>keep a limited record of correspondence where reasonably needed; and</li>
          <li>meet legal obligations that apply to the confirmed operator.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The form acknowledgement does not permit unrelated advertising, sale of contact details or adding you to a mailing list. If a newsletter or research programme is introduced, it will need a separate, specific explanation and choice.</p>
        <p>The lawful basis for each use must be identified in the approved notice after the operating entity and applicable jurisdiction are confirmed.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>4. Sharing and service providers</h2>
        <p>Enquiry data is processed and stored by Netlify as the website host and form provider. It may also be included in an email notification if that feature is enabled. Authorised people supporting Impact Sol. may access a message when needed to respond or maintain the system.</p>
        <p>No provider should use enquiry information for its own advertising. The final notice must name or clearly categorise production providers, their processing locations, contractual safeguards and any legally required disclosures.</p>
        <p>Information may also need to be disclosed where a confirmed operator is required to do so by law, or to protect people and systems from fraud, abuse or a serious security threat. The exact wording requires legal review.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>5. Retention and security</h2>
        <p>Production owners must approve a retention period and regularly export or delete Netlify form submissions to apply it. A message may need to be retained longer if it becomes part of continuing correspondence or a legal record, subject to an approved retention policy.</p>
        <p>The site is designed to use encrypted transport in production, browser validation, Netlify spam filtering, a hidden spam trap and restricted dashboard access. No internet service can promise absolute security. If a material incident affects personal information, the confirmed operator should follow the notification duties that apply to it.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="choices" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>6. Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>You can choose not to submit a form and use the published email route instead. You can also ask to access, correct or delete information connected to your enquiry. Other rights—such as restriction, objection, portability or complaint to a regulator—depend on the law that applies to the confirmed operator and to you.</p>
        <p>Send a request to <a href={mailto}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>. Enough information may be requested to locate the record and confirm that a request is legitimate; do not email unnecessary identity documents. The approved notice must state response periods, exceptions and the relevant supervisory authority.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>7. Cookies, analytics and external links</h2>
        <p>This launch build does not enable non-essential analytics, advertising tags or marketing cookies. Basic server logs and browser storage strictly necessary for security or service operation may still be used by the final hosting setup and must be documented.</p>
        <p>If optional analytics or embedded third-party media are introduced, they should remain off until the notice, consent mechanism and vendor review are updated where required.</p>
        <p>Links to third-party websites are governed by those services’ own privacy practices. A link does not mean Impact Sol. controls or endorses that service.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Children</h2>
        <p>These public enquiry forms are not designed to collect information from children. The final operator must define any age threshold and procedure required by its jurisdiction and product scope. If you believe a child has submitted personal information, use the privacy contact route so the situation can be reviewed.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Changes to this notice</h2>
        <p>The reviewed date will change when this notice is materially updated. Important changes should be explained clearly, and additional notice or consent should be sought if required by applicable law.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>10. Privacy contact</h2>
        <p>Email <a href={mailto}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with “Privacy request” in the subject line. This is a provisional contact route until the responsible legal entity and formal privacy address are published.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-status {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-sun);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: var(--color-mint-soft);
  }

  .legal-status span { color: var(--color-muted); }

  .legal-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 16rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .legal-layout > aside {
    position: sticky;
    top: 7rem;
  }

  .legal-layout nav {
    display: grid;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .legal-layout nav a {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    align-items: center;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .legal-copy { max-width: 52rem; }
  .legal-copy section { padding-block: 0 2.5rem; scroll-margin-top: 7rem; }
  .legal-copy section + section { padding-top: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .legal-copy h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); }
  .legal-copy h3 { margin-top: var(--space-5); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .legal-copy p, .legal-copy li { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .legal-copy li + li { margin-top: 0.55rem; }

  @media (max-width: 50rem) {
    .legal-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .legal-layout > aside { position: static; }
    .legal-status { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
